{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["The sense of <b>So Cain went out from the presence of HaShem</b> is that he never again stood before Him, as in the expression \"and from Your presence I will hide.\" And the sense of \"and settled in the land of Nod\" is that he did not roam throughout the entire world, but in that land he dwelt wandering continually, never resting in any single place within it at all; and it is called \"the land of Nod\" after his name forever."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:35.433653093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}